# Whitelist: ignore everything at the project root, then allow only our own work.
# This keeps the third-party clones (CAI-modified, caldera, hexstrike-ai, kit,
# stealth-browser-mcp, 5.3.0, MCPHost-modifed, mcp-cli, ...) and local tooling out.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/RedBlue-MultiAgent/
!/CyberTuringAgnet/
!/Benchmark/
!/Research-Paper resources/
!/Langchain/
!/rag/
!/mitre-attack-kb/
!/cwe-kb/
!/capec-kb/
!/cisa-kev-kb/
!/d3fend-kb/
!/owasp-cheatsheets-kb/
!/findings/

# --- Local cleanup and working notes (kept on disk, never pushed)
_local_cleanup/
Research-Paper resources/PAPER-GAPS-FOR-FIXING.md

# --- Sensitive or withheld material
# The paper states the red-team prompts are withheld; never publish them.
Benchmark/CyberMetric/offensive_cybersecurity_red_team_100_prompts.csv
# Personal screenshots
*.jpeg
*.jpg
# Local chat history database
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Secrets
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.tlp

# --- Third-party data and generated artifacts that can be rebuilt
CVE-fetching-Agent/
*-kb/raw/
rag/rag_corpus.jsonl

# --- Python / tooling caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.playwright-mcp/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/

# --- LaTeX build outputs (the PDF itself is kept)
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls

# --- Backups and OS files
*.bak
paper_backup*.tex
paper_before*.tex
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
